  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). PARTLY STALE: core premise holds; the carried action is done.\n- No code, playbook or hook detects ENOSPC or checks free space (grep of scripts/, .agent/ playbooks and hooks, packages/*/src finds only I/O-catalogue rows). /tmp is still a 12G tmpfs holding agent scratchpads. No script implements \"parallel measurement agents\": they are ad-hoc Agent-tool fan-outs.\n- DONE: the ACTION ITEM CARRIED. INV-busis's thread has the full five-repo figure (137 blocked / 68 production, naming the ENOSPC loss), and INV-busis is satisfied since 2026-09-09. No ENOSPC recurrence found after the 08-09 entry.\n- PARTIAL MITIGATIONS: the out-of-repo lab-notebook script decontend/slot refuses compute jobs when $HOME has < 2 GB free (MIN_DISK_GB, line 101) and tells agents to write to real disk, but it only REPORTS /tmp usage and says nothing about cohort reporting. scripts/check-measurement-frame (d181602ff7) requires committed records to declare a cohort key; it checks presence, not that every repo completed, and does not cover numbers posted in tracker threads (the busis case).\n- Mitigation 1 is unimplemented anywhere. Possible re-scope: \"fan-outs report attempted vs completed cohort; an instrument fails loudly when a repo's output is missing\"."  # 8eea
- op: discuss  # 3015
  at: '2026-10-03T08:03:09Z'  # 3015
  by: agent  # 3015
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3015
  clock: 3  # 3015
  nonce: '3015'  # 3015
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 on branch jgstern-agent/fix/kovoj (worktree ~/hg_wt/kovoj), commit f5730a1fe0. Not pushed.\n\nPREMISE, re-verified at the fix site. The truncation is not only in ad-hoc fan-outs: the shipped multi-repo instruments in scripts/ lost a member silently themselves. Two shapes:\n- DROPPED: `except Exception: print(stderr); continue`, totals over survivors, exit 0 (measure-blind-language-signal, measure-symbol-id-colon-conformance). BASELINE run of dev's measure-symbol-id-colon-conformance.py on [flask.json, a 3000-byte truncated copy, a missing file]: exit 0, TOTAL computed over 1 map, the two losses only as \"UNREADABLE\" stderr lines.\n- ZEROED: suppress(SystemExit) around in-process cli.main() then `report = {}` (row-inflation, cross-function-reach, escape-closing-ceiling, sanitizer-module-slot-ab, ctor-root-typing-ab, catalogue-reach), or a file walk over a missing path read as \"0 files\" (factory-receiver-shape, dotted-ctor-resolution-ab, ctor-table-derivation-ab, go-receiver-typing-gap, go-composite-literal-ab). BASELINE: dev's measure-row-inflation.py CLAIMS flask-restful /nonexistent/kserve printed \"kserve ... EXCLUDED - 0 cross_function findings (0 findings)\", exit 0; dev's measure-factory-receiver-shape.py printed \"kserve (0 py files)\", exit 0.\n\nFIX. scripts/lib/cohort_ledger.py: CohortLedger records covered / failed (with error) / not_attempted per member and continues past a failure (aborting invites a re-run with the member removed, which is the silent shrink). All 12 cohort instruments now print \"COHORT: covered K of N given ...\" naming each uncovered member, write the claim under \"cohort\" in their JSON, and exit 4 when K != N. run_cli_json raises MemberAbsent when a CLI run writes no report (exit code is not the test); read_json_member on missing/empty/truncated maps; require_dir on non-directories. Disk full is flagged DISK FULL, including when cli.main catches the OSError and prints \"internal error ... This is a bug\".\n\nEVIDENCE (live, branch, same inputs): row-inflation, cross-function-reach, escape-closing-ceiling, dotted-ctor, ctor-table, factory, go-receiver, go-composite -> \"COHORT: covered 1 of 2 given repo(s) -- INCOMPLETE\", exit 4; blind-language and symbol-id-colon on the 3 maps -> \"covered 1 of 3 given map(s)\", truncated map named \"not valid JSON ... truncated by a full disk?\", exit 4. Full-cohort controls exit 0 (\"covered 1 of 1 -- complete\"). Live ENOSPC: survey --out onto a symlink to /dev/full inside a ledger -> FAILED \"... OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device ... [DISK FULL -- check df -h ...]\", disk_full true in JSON, exit 4. Tests: tests/test_cohort_ledger.py (25 tests incl. one through the real verify-claims CLI, and a guard that every scripts/ file with a positional repos/maps nargs argument constructs a CohortLedger); red first (ModuleNotFoundError, then the guard red before wiring); smart-test affected run 5259 passed, 1 skipped, 2 xfailed, 0 failed.\n\nNOT DONE / NOT CLAIMED: bakeoff-broad/deep and dead-code-prospector-run (cohort via --repos) are outside the guard; ad-hoc Agent fan-outs (the filed busis case) have no script; mitigation 1's prompt text belongs in .agent/ playbooks (governance). Two instruments (sanitizer-module-slot-ab, ctor-root-typing-ab) crash in their positive controls on dev from stale monkeypatch signatures, so their cohort path was not exercised live. Residual items filed.\n\n\nRESIDUALS FILED: WI-bomos-lujib-mibok-jadud-hajip-fikih-kijar-bonaf (two A/B instruments crash on stale monkeypatch signatures), WI-huhip-hirif-dalas-dinal-sulov-rutaz-godav-zuvad (CLI labels ENOSPC \"This is a bug\"), WI-vivof-zatop-lidis-kosiv-rozod-kadad-mosof-kifuv (prospector + bakeoff cohort runners outside the ledger)."  # 3015
